      </h2>

      <p>
        Most heating advice online is written for a national audience, which
        means it often assumes winters much colder than ours. What works in
        Minnesota or Colorado does not always apply to homes in Bellingham and
        Whatcom County.
      </p>

      <p>
        Our climate is mild, damp, and coastal. Heating systems spend much of
        the winter running lightly, then suddenly work at full capacity during
        Fraser outflow events. Those conditions create a very different pattern
        of breakdowns than colder parts of the country.
      </p>

      <p>
        That is why our articles focus on the problems we actually see every
        week—older homes with retrofitted ductwork, twenty-year-old furnaces,
        heat pumps, airflow issues, and deciding honestly whether a repair
        still makes financial sense.
